How to shut off water to a house in an emergency: 3 steps	sample data
By Dana Ruiz · Master plumber, Harbor Plumbing · Published 19 Oct 2026 · 5 min read Sample	sample data: the name, line, date and minutes are the sample's (hosted.published)
Sample counts	sample data: the board's own Sample tag
Find your main shut-off valve, usually where the water line enters the house or in a box near the street, and close it: turn a lever a quarter turn so it sits across the pipe, or a round wheel clockwise until it stops. Then open the lowest faucet to drain the pipes and switch off the water heater.	sample data
Key takeaways Sample	sample data: the board's own Sample tag
Most homes have one main valve, where the supply line enters: often by the water heater, in the garage, or in a box near the curb.	sample data
A lever valve is closed when the handle sits across the pipe; a wheel valve closes clockwise.	sample data
The valve inside the curb box beside the meter may belong to the water utility. If yours will not close, call the utility’s emergency number on your bill.	sample data
After the water is off, turn off the water heater’s power or gas so it does not heat an empty tank.	sample data
